github.com/belluikit/goffmpeg-libs/linux_amd64
==============================================

FFmpeg (https://ffmpeg.org) built for linux_amd64 as shared libraries, so that an app
ships them and a user can replace them (LGPL 2.1 section 6b), in two codec
sets (belluikit/goffmpeg#41). An app's binary loads one of them.

shared/ holds the media set, which on desktop keeps every decoder, demuxer
and parser FFmpeg has, and one input device, for webcam capture.

  libavcodec-goffmpeg.so.63 libavdevice-goffmpeg.so.63 libavformat-goffmpeg.so.63 libavutil-goffmpeg.so.61 libswresample-goffmpeg.so.7 libswscale-goffmpeg.so.10

shared-audio/ holds the audio set: MP3 and WAV, with no libswscale and no
libavdevice.

  libavcodec-goffmpeg-audio.so.63 libavformat-goffmpeg-audio.so.63 libavutil-goffmpeg-audio.so.61 libswresample-goffmpeg-audio.so.7

lib/ contains libgoffmpeg.so, goffmpeg's purego bridge (see Bridge below).

FFmpeg version: N-125841-ge2bc6d88cd (git revision e2bc6d88cd68184288c16570e04881c3a426a05a).
No local patches: goffmpeg's build applies patches/*.patch to the FFmpeg
checkout, and goffmpeg has no such files (BUILDING.md: "The directory is
currently empty").

License: GNU Lesser General Public License, version 2.1 or later. The full
text is in LICENSE at the root of this repository, and is included in this
module's zip by the go command. The build used neither --enable-gpl nor
--enable-nonfree; each library reports "license: LGPL version 2.1 or later".

Configure line of shared/, as recorded in its libavutil (avutil_configuration()).

  --prefix=/linux_amd64 --extra-cflags=-fPIC --enable-pic --disable-autodetect --disable-programs --disable-doc --disable-debug --disable-encoders --disable-muxers --disable-avfilter --enable-swscale --enable-swresample --enable-network --arch=x86_64 --target-os=linux --enable-openssl --enable-avdevice --disable-indevs --enable-indev=v4l2 --enable-shared --disable-static --build-suffix=-goffmpeg

Configure line of shared-audio/, as recorded in its libavutil.

  --prefix=/linux_amd64 --extra-cflags=-fPIC --enable-pic --disable-autodetect --disable-programs --disable-doc --disable-debug --disable-encoders --disable-muxers --disable-avfilter --enable-swscale --enable-swresample --enable-network --arch=x86_64 --target-os=linux --enable-openssl --enable-avdevice --disable-decoders --disable-demuxers --disable-parsers --disable-bsfs --disable-hwaccels --disable-indevs --enable-demuxer='mp3,wav' --enable-decoder='mp3float,pcm_s16le,pcm_s24le,pcm_s32le,pcm_f32le,pcm_f64le,pcm_u8' --enable-parser=mpegaudio --disable-swscale --disable-avdevice --disable-videotoolbox --enable-shared --disable-static --build-suffix=-goffmpeg-audio

Corresponding source:
  FFmpeg:  https://github.com/belluikit/ffmpeg/tree/goffmpeg-e2bc6d88cd
           belluikit's mirror of FFmpeg. The tag is commit
           e2bc6d88cd68184288c16570e04881c3a426a05a and stays for as long as
           libraries built from it are published.
  Build:   https://github.com/belluikit/goffmpeg (Makefile, BUILDING.md), which
           pins that revision and these configure lines.
  Bridge:  lib/libgoffmpeg.* is goffmpeg's bridge.c (BSD-3-Clause), built by
           goffmpeg's 'make bridge-shared'. It holds no FFmpeg code: it loads
           the media set in shared/, looking beside itself and in ../shared.
           The current lib/libgoffmpeg.* was built from goffmpeg commit
           0d3e275 by GitHub Actions run 42778052636.
  Shared:  shared/ was built by goffmpeg's 'make dist' (SET=media) from
           goffmpeg commit 2e781bd by GitHub Actions run 42800313247.
           shared-audio/ was built by 'make dist SET=audio' from goffmpeg
           commit 0d3e275 by GitHub Actions run 42778052636.
           Both were built on Ubuntu 22.04 (glibc 2.35, the oldest
           goffmpeg supports).
